senses.gloss:
नीर् नीर् (नि-ईर्), Caus. P. नीरयति, -यितुम्,
to drive or impel into, urge forwards (to an aim);
to send forth, appoint (to a business).

निरक्ष निर्-अक्ष, अस्, आ, अम्, having no dice;
having no latitude; (अस्), m. (in astronomy) the
place of no latitude, i. e. the terrestrial equator.
—निरक्ष-देश, अस्, m. a first meridian, as Laṅkā;
a place where the sun is always vertical and the days
and nights are equal; the equatorial region.

नि-रत, अस्, आ, अम्, engaged or interested in;
attached or devoted to; pleased, delighted; rested,
ceased.

निरर्थ निर्-अर्थ, अस्, m. loss, detriment;
nonsense; (अस्, आ, अम्), destitute of wealth, poor;
useless; meaningless, unmeaning, nonsensical, pur-
poseless, vain; (a consonant is called निर्-अर्थ, not
fulfilling its purpose if it is not followed by a vowel.)
—निरर्थ-ता, f. senselessness, nonsense.

निरवलम्ब निर्-अवलम्ब, अस्, आ, अम्, having
no prop or stay; unsupported; not affording support;
not depending or relying on.

निरष्ट निर्-अष्ट, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. अश् or
अक्ष् with निस्), Ved. deprived of vigour, exhausted;
(Sāy.) = निर्-आकृत, driven away, scattered, dispersed.

निर्-अस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, ejecting, throwing out;
expelling; abandoning, neglecting, scattering, de-
stroying, &c.

निरहङ्कार निर्-अहङ्कार, अस्, आ, अम्, free
from egotism, devoid of selfishness, free from pride,
humble, lowly.

निरामय निर्-आमय, अस्, अम्, m. n. freedom
from illness, health, happiness, welfare; (अस्, आ, अम्),
free from illness, healthy, well, hale, recovered from
sickness, free from disease; free from taint, pure;
guileless; free from defects or failings; infallible;
not liable to failure or miscarriage; complete, full;
(अस्), m. a wild goat; a hog, a boar; N. of a king.

निरालोक निर्-आलोक, अस्, आ, अम्, not looking
about, not moving the eye, without moving the eyes;
deprived of light, dark; invisible, uninvestigable (?);
an epithet of Śiva.

निर्-ईक्षण, अस्, आ, अम्, looking at, regarding;
(अम्), ṇ. look; looking at, regarding, seeing; ex-
pecting; the aspect of the planets.

निर्-ऋथ, अस्, m. destruction, the Destroyer (i. e.
Nirṛtha personified); an epithet of a particular Agni;
(according to some) the Sāma-veda.

निर्जि निर्-जि, cl. 1. P. A. -जयति, -ते, -जेतुम्,
to conquer, win, gain, acquire, subdue, vanquish;
to overcome in play.

निर्-णेतृ, ता, त्री, तृ, decisive, certifying, veri-
fying, leading to certainty, demonstrating, proving;
(ता), m. one who pronounces a sentence, a judge;
a voucher; a guide.
—निर्णेतृ-त्व, अम्, n. proof,
verification.

निर्धाव् 1. निर्-धाव्, cl. 1. P. A. -धावति,
-ते, -धावितुम्, to stream forth from, spring from;
to run out, escape from.

निर्-बाध, अस्, m., Ved. a knob, prominence;
(निर्बाधे कृ is perhaps a proverbial expression
meaning ‘to put on one side, set aside, remove.’)

निर्मक्षिक निर्-मक्षिक, अस्, आ, अम्, free
from flies, free from tormentors, untroubled; (अम्),
n. the being free from flies; (अम्), ind. without flies.

निर्माख्य निर्-माख्य, अस्, m., N. of a man;
(probably a wrong form, also read तिग्मात्मन् and
निर्माद्.)

निर्मुट निर्-मुट, अस्, m. a tree bearing
large blossoms (= वनस्-पति); the sun; a rogue;
(अस्, अम्), m. n. a large and free market or fair.

निर्-लेप, अस्, आ, अम्, unanointed, unsmeared,
free from fatty substances; stainless, spotless, sinless;
(अस्), m. a sage.

1. निर्-वाद, अस्, m. (for 2. निर्-वाद see p. 501, col.
1), obloquy, censure, blame, reproach; rumour, report;
asseveration, affirmation, decision of a controversy.

2. निर्-वापित, अस्, आ, अम् (for 1. see under निर्-
वप्, p. 500, col. 2), extinguished, put out, quenched;
allayed, cooled; killed.

3. निर्-वाप्य, ind. (for 1. and 2. see under निर्-
वप्, p. 500, col. 2), having extinguished or quenched;
having refreshed or delighted.

निर्वयनी निर्-वयनी, f. the cast off skin
of a snake; (a various reading for निर्-व्लयनी;
cf. निर्-ल्वयनी.)

निर्-वाह, अस्, m. carrying on, accomplishing, per-
forming, managing, accomplishment, management;
completion, end; narrating, describing; supporting,
maintaining; subsisting on; sufficiency, adequacy,
competent provision or means of living; steadfastness;
[cf. नैर्वाहिक.]

निर्विघ्न निर्-विघ्न, अस्, आ, अम्, unobstructed,
uninterrupted, untroubled, secure from impediments;
(अम्), n. absence of obstruction or impediment;
(अम् or एन), ind. unobstructedly, freely, securely.

निर्-विष्ट, अस्, आ, अम्, attained, arrived at, met
with; obtained, gained, experienced, earned, received;
engaged in, occupied by, staying in; married.

निर्-वृति, इस्, f. complete satisfaction, contentment,
tranquillity, bliss, happiness, gladness, pleasure; final
emancipation or liberation from existence; freedom;
rest, repose; setting, disappearance, death, destruc-
tion; completion, accomplishment (for निर्-वृत्ति);
ceasing, abstaining from (for नि-वृत्ति); incivility,
impropriety (for निर्-वृत्ति); (इस्), m., N. of a man;
of a son of Vṛṣṇi; (the forms निर्-वृति, निर्-
वृत्ति, and नि-वृत्ति are often incorrectly confounded
together.)

निर्वैर निर्-वैर, अम्, n. absence of enmity;
(अस्, आ, अम्), free from enmity, without enmity,
living in peace, peaceable; (अस्), m., N. of a hunter;
(अम्), ind. peaceably, without enmity.
—निर्वैर-ता,
f. freedom from enmity, peaceableness, concord.

निर्वोढृ निर्-वोढृ, ढा, ढ्री, ढृ, car-
rying or leading away, who or what carries away;
separating, dividing; [cf. निर्-वहितृ.]

निर्-व्यूढ, अस्, आ, अम्, finished, completed;
abandoned, left, deserted; (अम्), n. various reading
for निर्-वाह, completion.

निर्-हारिन्, ई, इणी, इ, taking forth or out, carrying
out; diffusively fragrant, spreading wide (as odour);
having wealth.

नीरूप नी-रूप, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. निस् + रूप),
formless, shapeless, mis-shapen; (अस्), m. air, wind;
a god; (अम्), n. heaven, ether.
